  "finalText": "Done. All route-related tests pass identically (same 2 pre-existing failures in unrelated modules).\n\n**What changed:** In `src/routes/routeHelpers.ts:16-23`, `asyncHandler` now composes `wrapAsync` instead of duplicating its try/catch:\n\n```ts\n// Before: duplicated try/catch\nexport function asyncHandler(handler) {\n  return async (req, res, next) => {\n    try {\n      if (!req.user) { /* 401 */ return; }\n      await handler(req, res);\n    } catch (error: any) {\n      res.status(error.statusCode || 500).json({ error: error.message });\n    }\n  };\n}\n\n// After: composes wrapAsync\nexport function asyncHandler(handler) {\n  return wrapAsync(async (req, res) => {\n    if (!req.user) { /* 401 */ return; }\n    await handler(req, res);\n  });\n}\n```\n\nError handling now lives in one place (`wrapAsync`). `asyncHandler` adds the auth check on top. No observable behavior change.",
